===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|biology|systematics}} The study of the [[evolutionary]] history and [[relationship]]s among or within groups of [[organism]]s, through [[computational]] methods that focus on observed [[heritable]] traits.
#* {{quote-journal|en|{{w|William Morton Wheeler}}|year=''[[circa#Latin|c.]]'' 1899|George Baur’s Life and Writings|The American Naturalist|volume=33|page=16|text=Thereupon he went to Leipzig, and during the winter of 1880–81 and the following summer semester studied comparative anatomy with Leuckart, geology with Credner, and '''phylogenetics''' with Carus.}}
#* '''2005''', Stephen Bryant, Gerard Bouffard, ''Bioinformatics'', Wiley, [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=Us9pAAAAMAAJ&q=%22An+especially+concise+introduction+to+molecular+phylogenetics+is+provided+by+Hillis+et+al.+(1993).+The+danger+of+generating+incorrect+results+is+inherently+greater+in+computational+phylogenetics+than+in+many+other+fields+of+science.%22&dq=%22An+especially+concise+introduction+to+molecular+phylogenetics+is+provided+by+Hillis+et+al.+(1993).+The+danger+of+generating+incorrect+results+is+inherently+greater+in+computational+phylogenetics+than+in+many+other+fields+of+science.%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwj5nsr8wJ79AhVhcWwGHfGmAocQ6AF6BAgHEAI page 366],
